From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 12:07:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 052/184] segacd: D: -- a filesystem read off the compact disc

A blocking reader on stage 3's machinery, a CD bus in the disk layer,
and 512-byte GEMDOS blocks mapped onto 2048-byte CD sectors with one
sector cached. Four consecutive blocks come out of one read, and a
sector already on its way is waited for rather than seeked to: a seek
is most of a second and a streamed sector is thirteen milliseconds, so
re-seeking per block would be four seconds for every two kilobytes.

Three things were wrong in the first cut, and the console said all
three:

- It kept commanding. The read command stayed queued after the drive
  started reading, so 'begin at this position' went out seventy-five
  times a second for as long as D: was mounted. Stage 2's lesson
  upside down: the conversation needs a turn every exchange, and it
  needs the right one.
- The self-test ran in the VBL, at interrupt level 3, blocking the 200
  Hz tick and tripping the CDD storm guard, which counts drive
  interrupts between VBLs. It runs in foreground now.
- The sector cache outlived the drive moving. cdc_setup() invalidates
  it, because whoever re-initialises the decoder is also moving the
  head.
